  "pass_a_gloss": "Upon the much-discussed question we have come to see what is the partridge, concerning which the Scripture now says: 'The partridge called, gathered what it did not bear, making its wealth not with judgment. In the middle of its days they will abandon it, and at its end it will be foolish.' From the treatise on the nature of animals we must take what is recounted about the partridge, so that knowing the things about the animal we may know whether to rank the partridge said now upon a better or worse rank. It is said indeed to be an animal most wicked, and deceitful, and altogether crafty, and intending to deceive those hunting it and often rolling about the feet of the hunter, so that it may surround it as being near the animal in order not to come upon the net. And whenever it intends to have surrounded the hunter and the young have fled, then it also flies away. But the animal is exceedingly unclean, so that the males fight one another concerning mating and males mount males. If therefore it is wicked and unclean and altogether crafty and deceitful, this animal being such, it is clear that to rank it upon a better and to say it can be referred upon the Savior appears impious. Therefore we must see, if we wish to interpret it upon the opposite, whether the whole interpretation follows us.",
